Licensing and rights
====================

Corpus-authored material
------------------------

Original metadata, navigation files, capsules, and claim or Q&A records that
are explicitly marked as human-reviewed are licensed under the Creative
Commons Attribution 4.0 International license (CC BY 4.0):

https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Software and scripts in this repository may be used under the same CC BY 4.0
terms unless a file says otherwise.

Any valid license or dedication previously granted for an earlier version of
repository-authored material remains effective for that earlier version.

Scholarly works
----------------

Article text, accepted manuscripts, publisher versions, and PDF files retain
their source- or publisher-specific copyright and license terms. Their presence
in this repository does not place them in the public domain and does not grant
rights beyond those supplied by the relevant author, repository, or publisher.
Consult the per-paper metadata and the linked source before reuse.

No additional rights are granted in third-party material, trademarks, names,
images, or other content not owned by the licensor.
